# Walkthrough - Nextcloud Trusted Domains Update

I have successfully updated the `trusted_domains` configuration for your Nextcloud instance on ZimaOS.

## Changes Made

- Added `zimaos.local` to the trusted domains list.
- Added `192.168.1.168` to the trusted domains list as requested.
- Added `192.168.1.186` (the current server IP) to ensure consistent access.

## Verification

I executed the following commands via SSH:

```bash
sudo docker exec --user www-data nextcloud php occ config:system:set trusted_domains 2 --value="zimaos.local"
sudo docker exec --user www-data nextcloud php occ config:system:set trusted_domains 3 --value="192.168.1.168"
sudo docker exec --user www-data nextcloud php occ config:system:set trusted_domains 4 --value="192.168.1.186"
```

The final trusted domains list is:
1. `http://192.168.1.186:10081`
2. `http://192.168.0.1`
3. `zimaos.local`
4. `192.168.1.168`
5. `192.168.1.186`

You should now be able to access Nextcloud through any of these addresses without the "Untrusted Domain" error.
